{"event": "llm_start", "tag": "write", "prompt": "This PyTorch function is part of a model being trained. It is too slow to train with:\n\n```python\nimport torch\nCHANNEL_DECAY = True\n\ndef reference(q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma, scale):\n    B, H, T, K = q.shape\n    V = v.shape[-1]\n    q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma = (x.to(torch.promote_types(x.dtype, torch.float32)) for x in (q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma))\n    S = q.new_zeros(B, H, K, V)\n    outs = []\n    for t in range(T):\n        kt, vt, et, bt = (k[:, :, t], v[:, :, t], e[:, :, t], beta[:, :, t])\n        ct = gamma[:, :, t]\n        S = S * g[:, :, t].exp()[..., None]\n        S = S - ct[..., None, None] * et[..., None] * (S * et[..., None]).sum(-2)[..., None, :]\n        pred = (S * kt[..., None]).sum(-2)\n        S = S + (bt[..., None] * (vt - pred))[..., None, :] * kt[..., None]\n        outs.append((S * (q[:, :, t] * scale)[..., None]).sum(-2))\n    return torch.stack(outs, dim=2)\n\n```\n\nThe model calls it like this (shapes, dtypes and strides as observed):\n\n    muse_jobs.j_7ccb685993cf2333a0b3df9d.reference(Tensor(shape=[2, 2, 64, 16], dtype=bfloat16, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 2, 64, 16], dtype=bfloat16, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 2, 64, 16], dtype=bfloat16, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 2, 64, 16], dtype=bfloat16, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 2, 64, 16], dtype=float32, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 2, 64], dtype=float32, contiguous), Tensor(shape=[2, 2, 64], dtype=float32, contiguous), 0.25)\n\nObserved on every call:\n- k and e have unit-norm rows\n- g <= 0\n- beta and gamma lie in [0,1]\n\nIt takes 8 ms forward on this call. Target environment: {'cache_version': 2, 'python': '3.12.3', 'torch': '2.8.0+cu128', 'triton': '3.4.0', 'cuda': '12.8', 'platform': 'Linux', 'gpu': [{'name': 'NVIDIA L4', 'capability': [8, 9], 'memory': 23661248512}]}.\nWrite a fast Triton implementation for that environment.\n\nRequirements:\n- Define `def kernel_function(q, k, v, e, g, beta, gamma, scale):` with the same arguments and semantics, returning the same result.\n- It must match the function on any inputs it accepts within the observed constraints.\n- The computation must happen in your own @triton.jit kernels; the Python wrapper may only allocate, reshape,\n  launch and do cheap elementwise prep. Do not import or copy any existing implementation.\n\nYou cannot run anything. Return the complete module in one ```python block, then 2-4 sentences on your\napproach and anything you are unsure about.", "t": 1793132292.867877}
